1
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:07,960
Wonder by R. J. Palacio.

2
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,520
Part 8. August.

3
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:18,800
You're going to reach the sky. Fly, beautiful child. your Rhythmix, beautiful child.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,320
the fifth grade nature retreat.

5
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:25,560
EVERY YEAR IN the spring,, the fifth graders of Beecher Prep go away for 3

6
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:30,200
days and 2 nights to a place called Broarwood Nature Reserve in

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,080
Pennsylvania.. It’s a 4-hour bus drive away..

8
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,640
The kids sleep in cabins with bunk beds..

9
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:40,760
There are campfires and s’mores and long walks through the woods..

10
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:45,360
The teachers have been prepping us about this all year long,. so, all the kids in

11
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,480
the grade are excited about it—.

12
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,080
—except for me..

13
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:51,600
And it’s not even that I’m not excited,,

14
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:56,640
because I kind of am—. —it’s just I’ve never slept away from home before. and

15
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,480
I’m kind of nervous..

16
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:02,920
Most kids have had sleepovers by the time they’re my age.. A lot of kids have

17
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:07,480
gone to sleepaway camps, or stayed with their grandparents or whatever..

18
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,720
Not me..

19
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,440
Not unless you include hospital stays,.

20
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:16,320
but even then, Mom or Dad always stayed with me overnight.. But I never slept

21
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:21,280
over at Tata and Papa's house, or Aunt Kate and Uncle Po’s house..

22
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:24,960
When I was really little,, that was mainly because there were too many

23
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:30,200
medical issues,. like my trach tube needing to be cleared every hour, or

24
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:35,560
reinserting my feeding tube if it got detached.. But when I got bigger,, I just

25
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:38,280
never felt like sleeping anywhere else..

26
00:01:38,280 --> 00:01:42,200
There was one time when I half slept over Christopher’s house..

27
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:46,600
We were about eight, and we were still best friends.. Our family had gone for a

28
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,200
visit to his house, and me and Christopher were having such a great

29
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:55,400
time playing Lego Star Wars that I didn’t want to leave when it was time to go..

30
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:00,520
We were like,, "“Please,, please,, please, can we have a sleepover?”?"

31
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:05,280
So, our parents said yes,. and Mom and Dad and Via drove home.. And me and

32
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:10,440
Christopher stayed up till midnight playing,, until Lisa,, his mom,, said:,

33
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:13,240
"“Okay,, guys,, time to go to bed.”."

34
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,320
Well,, that’s when I kind of panicked a bit..

35
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:20,600
Lisa tried to help me go to sleep,, but I just started crying that I wanted to go

36
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,760
home.. So, at 1:00 a...m.., Lisa called Mom

37
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:28,480
and Dad,, and Dad drove all the way back out to Bridgeport to pick me up..

38
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:31,160
We didn’t get home until 3:00 a...m..

39
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:36,880
So, my one and only sleepover,, up until now,, was pretty much of a disaster,,

40
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:40,560
which is why I’m a little nervous about the nature retreat..

41
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:45,320
On the other hand,, I’m really excited.

42
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,760
Known for.

43
00:02:46,760 --> 00:02:51,200
I ASKED MOM to buy me a new rolling duffel bag, because my old one had Star

44
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:55,800
Wars stuff on it,, and there was no way I was going to take that to the fifth

45
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,640
grade nature retreat..

46
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:03,040
As much as I love Star Wars, I didn't want that to be what I’m known for..

47
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:07,800
Everyone’s known for something in middle school.. Like, Reed is known for really

48
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:12,959
being into marine life and the oceans and things like that.. And Amos is known

49
00:03:12,959 --> 00:03:15,640
for being a really good baseball player..

50
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:20,280
And Charlotte is known for having been in a TV commercial when she was six..

51
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:23,720
And Zamina is known for being really smart..

52
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:28,600
My point is, that in middle school, you kind of get known for what you’re into,,

53
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,600
and you have to be careful about stuff like that..

54
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:37,320
Like, Max G and Max W will never live down their Dungeons and Dragons obsession..

55
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:42,360
So, I was actually trying to ease out of the whole Star Wars thing a bit.. I mean,,

56
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:46,640
it’ll always be special to me,, like it is with the doctor who, but in

57
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:52,600
my hearing aids., It’s just not the thing I wanted to be known for in middle school..

58
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:57,280
I’m not sure what I want to be known for,, but it’s not that..

59
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:02,360
That’s not exactly true:. I do know what I’m really known for.,

60
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:04,880
But there’s nothing I can do about that..

61
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:10,080
A Star Wars duffel bag I could do something about.

62
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,240
Packing.

63
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:15,600
MOM HELPED ME pack the night before the big trip.. We put all the clothes I was

64
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:21,440
taking on my bed,, and she folded everything neatly and put it inside the bag while I watched..

65
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:26,720
It was a plain blue rolling duffel,, by the way:. no logos or artwork..

66
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:31,680
"“What if I can’t sleep at night?”?" I asked.. "“Take a book with you.. Then if

67
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:35,640
you can’t sleep,, you can pull out your flashlight, and read for a bit until you

68
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:38,040
get sleepy,”." she answered..

69
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,280
I nodded..

70
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,440
"“What if I have a nightmare?”?"

71
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,480
"“Your teachers will be there,, sweetie,”."

72
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:47,520
she said.. "“And Jack., And your friends.”."

73
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:52,160
"“I can bring Babu." I said.. That was my favorite stuffed animal when I was

74
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:56,160
little., A small black bear with a soft black nose..

75
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:00,680
"“You don’t really sleep with him anymore,, do you?”?" said Mom..

76
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:04,720
"“No,, but I keep them in my closet in case I wake up in the middle of the

77
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:08,560
night and can’t get back to sleep,”." I said..

78
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:12,440
"“I could hide him in my bag.. No one would know.”."

79
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:18,000
"“Then let’s do that.”." Mom nodded,, getting Babu from inside my closet..

80
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,480
"“I wish they allowed cell phones,”." I said..

81
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:24,440
"“I know,, me too!”." she said..

82
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:27,720
"“Though I know you’re going to have a great time,, Auggie.."

83
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:30,520
"You sure you want me to pack Babu?"

84
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,760
"Yeah,."

85
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:34,280
"but way down where no one can see him,”."

86
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,680
I said..

87
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:40,200
She stuck Babu deep inside the bag and then stuffed the last of my T-shirts on

88
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:41,760
top of him..

89
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:45,560
"“So many clothes for just 2 days."

90
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:48,760
"3 days and 2 nights,”." I corrected her..

91
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,400
"“Yep.”." She nodded,, smiling..

92
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,840
"“Three days and two nights.”."

93
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:56,680
She zipped up the duffel bag and picked it up..

94
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:59,320
"“Not too heavy.." "Try it.”."

95
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:00,960
I picked up the bag..

96
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:03,120
"“Fine.”." I shrugged..

97
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:05,120
She sat on the bed..

98
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:09,640
"“Hey,, what happened to your Empire Strikes Back poster?”?"

99
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:15,160
"“Oh,, I took that down ages ago,”." I answered.. She shook her head..

100
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:18,520
"“Huh,, I didn’t notice that before.”."

101
00:06:18,520 --> 00:06:24,760
"“I’m trying to,, you know,, change my image a bit,”." I explained..

102
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:28,919
"“Okay.”." She smiled,, nodding like she understood..

103
00:06:28,919 --> 00:06:33,040
"“Anyway,, honey,, you have to promise me you won’t forget to put on the bug

104
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:38,280
spray,, okay?? On the legs,, especially when you’re hiking through the woods..

105
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:41,840
It’s right here in the front compartment.”." "“Uh-huh.”."

106
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:44,280
"“And put on your sunscreen,”." she said..

107
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:50,840
"“You do not want to get a sunburn.. And don’t,, I repeat,, do not forget to take

108
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:53,880
your hearing aids off if you go swimming.”."

109
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:56,080
"“Would I get electrocuted?”?"

110
00:06:56,080 --> 00:07:00,760
"“No,, but you’d be in real hot water with Daddy because those things cost a

111
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:03,480
fortune!”." she laughed..

112
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,760
"“I put the rain poncho in the front compartment,, too..

113
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,720
Same thing goes if it rains, Augie, okay??

114
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,919
Make sure you cover the hearing aids with the hood.”."

115
00:07:12,919 --> 00:07:16,240
"“Aye,, aye,, sir,”." I said,, saluting..

116
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,760
She smiled and pulled me over..

117
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:23,360
"“I can’t believe how much you’ve grown up this year, Augie." she said softly,,

118
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,600
putting her hands on the sides of my face..

119
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,880
"“Do I look taller?”?"

120
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,360
"“Definitely.”." She nodded..

121
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:34,320
"“I’m still the shortest one in my grade.”."

122
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:41,280
"“I’m not really even talking about your height,”." she said.. "“Suppose I hate it there?”."

123
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:44,440
"“You’re going to have a great time, Augie.

124
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:48,800
I nodded.. She got up and gave me a quick kiss on the forehead..

125
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:52,440
“Okay,, so I say we get to bed now.”.

126
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:57,720
“It’s only 9:00, Mom!”. “Your bus leaves at 6:00 a...m.. tomorrow..

127
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,360
You don’t want to be late..

128
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:02,760
Come on., Chop chop.. Your teeth are brushed?”?

129
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:07,640
I nodded and climbed into bed.. She started to lie down next to me..

130
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:11,480
“You don’t need to put me to bed tonight,, Mom,”. I said..

131
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:14,160
“I’ll read on my own till I get sleepy.”.

132
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,320
“Really?”?

133
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:20,280
She nodded,, impressed.. She squeezed my hand and gave it a kiss..

134
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:23,080
“Okay, then. Good night, love..

135
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,960
Have sweet dreams.”.

136
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,480
“You, too.”.

137
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:29,720
She turned on the little reading light beside the bed..

138
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:33,479
“I’ll write you letters,”, I said as she was leaving..

139
00:08:33,479 --> 00:08:37,599
“Even though I’ll probably be home before you guys even get them.”. “Then we can read

140
00:08:37,599 --> 00:08:39,840
them together,”, she said,.

141
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,840
and threw me a kiss..

142
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:46,920
When she left my room,, I took my copy of The Lion,, the Witch, and the Wardrobe

143
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:52,560
off the nightstand and started reading until I fell asleep..

144
00:08:52,560 --> 00:08:58,320
though the Witch knew the Deep Magic,, there is a magic deeper still which she did not know..

145
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:02,280
Her knowledge goes way back only to the dawn of time..

146
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:06,400
But if she could have looked a little further back, into the stillness and the

147
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:14,160
darkness before Time dawned,, she would have read there a different incantation.

148
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,600
Daybreak.

149
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:20,680
THE NEXT DAY I woke up really early.. It was still dark inside my room and even

150
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:24,760
darker outside,, though I knew it would be morning soon..

151
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:28,920
I turned over on my side but didn’t feel at all sleepy..

152
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,880
That’s when I saw Daisy sitting near my bed..

153
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:34,920
I mean,, I knew it wasn’t Daisy,, but for

154
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:38,800
a second I saw a shadow that looked like her..

155
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:43,640
I didn’t think it was a dream then,, but now,, looking back,, I know it must have

156
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:44,640
been..

157
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:47,360
It didn’t make me sad to see her at all:.

158
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,640
it just filled me up with nice feelings inside..

159
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:55,600
She was gone after a second,, and I couldn’t see her again in the darkness..

160
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:59,920
The room slowly started lightening.. I reached for my hearing aid headband and

161
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:04,680
put it on,, and now the world was really awake.. I could hear the garbage trucks

162
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:09,360
clanking down the street and the birds in our backyard.. And down the hallway, I

163
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:11,320
heard Mom’s alarm beeping..

164
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:17,240
Daisy’s ghost made me feel super strong inside,, knowing wherever I am,, she’d be

165
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,840
there with me..

166
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:21,080
I got up out of bed and went to my desk

167
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:24,920
and wrote a little note to Mom.. Then I went into the living room, where my

168
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:29,960
packed bag was by the door.. I opened it up and fished inside until I found what

169
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,640
I was looking for..

170
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,040
I took Baboo back to my room,, and I laid

171
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:39,120
him in my bed and taped the little note to Mom on his chest.. And then I covered

172
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:44,320
him with my blanket so Mom would find him later.. The note read:, "Dear Mom,, I

173
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:49,400
won’t need Baboo,, but if you miss me,, you can cuddle with him yourself.

174
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:52,600
XOXO, Auggie."

175
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:56,040
Day one. THE BUS RIDE went really fast..

176
00:10:56,040 --> 00:11:00,920
I sat by the window and Jack was next to me in the aisle seat.. Summer and Maya

177
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:02,440
were in front of us..

178
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:07,800
Everyone was in a good mood., Kind of loud,, laughing a lot.. I noticed right

179
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:12,440
away that Julian wasn’t on our bus,, even though Henry and Miles were..

180
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:16,880
I figured he must be on the other bus,, but then I overheard Miles tell Amos

181
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:20,320
that Julian ditched the grade trip because he thought the whole nature

182
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:24,680
retreat thing was,, {quote} {unquote,}, dorky..

183
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:29,120
I got totally pumped because dealing with Julian for 3 days in a row— —and two

184
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:34,240
nights— —was a major reason that I was nervous about this whole trip.. So, now

185
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:39,360
without him there,, I could really just relax and not worry about anything..

186
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:43,960
We got to the nature reserve at around noon.. The first thing we did was put our

187
00:11:43,960 --> 00:11:48,360
stuff down in the cabins.. There were three bunk beds to every room,, so me and

188
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:53,640
Jack did rock,, paper,, scissors for the top bunk, and I won. Woohoo! And the

189
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:58,000
other guys in the room were Reed and Tristan, and Pablo and Nino..

190
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,360
After we had lunch in the main cabin,, we all went on a two-hour guided nature

191
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:06,040
hike through the woods.. But these were not woods like the kind they have in

192
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,920
Central Park:. these were real woods..

193
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:13,760
Giant trees that almost totally blocked out the sunlight.. Tangles of leaves and

194
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:18,760
fallen tree trunks.. Howls and chirps and really loud bird calls.. There was a

195
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:24,600
slight fog,, too,, like a pale blue smoke all around us.. So cool..

196
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:29,160
The nature guide pointed everything out to us:. the different types of trees we

197
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:34,280
were passing,. the insects inside the dead logs on the trail,. the signs of

198
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:38,640
deer and bears in the woods,. what types of birds were whistling and where to

199
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:43,000
look for them.. I realized that my low-bot hearing aids actually made me

200
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:48,839
hear better than most people, because I was usually the first person to hear a new bird call..

201
00:12:48,839 --> 00:12:53,680
It started to rain as we headed back to camp.. I pulled on my rain poncho and

202
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:57,960
pulled the hood up so my hearing aids wouldn’t get wet,. but my jeans and shoes

203
00:12:57,960 --> 00:13:03,320
got soaked by the time we reached our cabins.. Everyone got soaked.. It was fun,,

204
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:07,960
though.. We had a wet sock fight in the cabin..

205
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:12,120
Since it rained for the rest of the day,, we spent most of the afternoon goofing

206
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:17,240
off in the rec room.. They had a ping pong table and old-style arcade games

207
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:22,080
like Pac-Man and Missile Command that we played until dinner time. Luckily,, by

208
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:27,160
then, it had stopped raining,, so we got to have a real campfire cookout.. The log

209
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:31,080
benches around the campfire were still a little damp,, but we threw our jackets

210
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:35,200
over them and hung out by the fire,, toasting s’mores and eating the best

211
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,800
roasted hot dogs I have ever, ever tasted..

212
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:40,840
Mom was right about the mosquitoes:.

213
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:44,800
there were tons of them.. But luckily, I had spritzed myself before I left the

214
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:49,240
cabin,, and I wasn’t eaten alive like some of the other kids were..

215
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:53,560
I loved hanging out by the campfire after dark.. I loved the way bits of fire

216
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:56,800
dust would float up and disappear into the night air..

217
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:59,480
And how the fire lit up people’s faces..

218
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,800
I loved the sound the fire made,, too..

219
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:06,000
And how the woods were so dark that you couldn’t see anything around you,. and

220
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,800
you’d look up and see a billion stars in

221
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:12,760
the sky.. The sky doesn’t look like that in North River Heights..

222
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:15,480
I’ve seen it look like that in Montauk,, though:.

223
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:20,680
like someone sprinkled salt on a shiny black table..

224
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,640
I was so tired when I got back to the

225
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:27,280
cabin, and I didn’t need to pull out the book to read.. I fell asleep almost as

226
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:29,560
fast as my head hit the pillow..

227
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,400
And maybe I dreamed about the stars,.

228
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:35,040
I don’t know.

229
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,760
The fairgrounds.

230
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:41,120
THE NEXT DAY was just as great as the first day.. We went horseback riding in

231
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:46,000
the morning,, and in the afternoon, we repelled up some ginormous trees with

232
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,120
the help of the nature guides..

233
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:53,240
By the time we got back to the cabins for dinner,, we were all really tired again..

234
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:57,320
After dinner, they told us we had an hour to rest,, and then we were going to

235
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:02,680
take a 15-minute bus ride to the fairgrounds for an outdoor movie night..

236
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,040
I hadn’t had the chance to write a

237
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:08,280
letter to Mom and Dad and Via yet,. so, I wrote one telling them all about the

238
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:11,080
stuff we did that day and the day before..

239
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:15,200
I pictured myself reading it to them out loud when I got back,, since there was

240
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:18,600
just no way the letter would get home before I did..

241
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:23,160
When we got to the fairgrounds,, the sun was just starting to set.. It was about

242
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:27,600
7:30. The shadows were really long on the grass, and the clouds were pink and

243
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:32,720
orange.. It looked like someone had taken sidewalk chalk and smudged

244
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:37,080
the colors across the sky with their fingers.. It’s not that I haven’t seen

245
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:42,400
nice sunsets before in the city, because I have—. —slivers of sunsets between

246
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:48,200
buildings—. —but I wasn’t used to seeing so much sky in every direction.. Out here

247
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:52,360
in the fairgrounds,, I could understand why ancient people used to think the

248
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:55,000
world was flat and the sky was a dome

249
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,440
that closed in on top of it.. That’s what it looked like from the fairgrounds, in

250
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:02,200
the middle of this huge open field..

251
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:06,040
Because we were the first school to arrive,, we got to run around the field

252
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:10,200
all we wanted until the teachers told us it was time to lay out our sleeping bags

253
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:13,160
on the ground and get good viewing seats..

254
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:17,520
We unzipped our bags and laid them down like picnic blankets on the grass in

255
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:20,880
front of the giant movie screen in the middle of the field..

256
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:24,240
Then we went to the row of food trucks parked at the edge of the field to load

257
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,240
up on snacks and sodas and stuff like that..

258
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:31,400
There were concession stands there,, too,, like at a farmers’ market,, selling

259
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,720
roasted peanuts and cotton candy..

260
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:38,040
And up a little farther was a short row of carnival-type stalls,, the kind where

261
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:42,240
you can win a stuffed animal if you throw a baseball into a basket..

262
00:16:42,240 --> 00:16:47,760
Jack and I both tried— —and failed— —to win anything,. but we heard Amos won a yellow

263
00:16:47,760 --> 00:16:50,920
hippo and gave it to Zamina.

264
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:55,920
That was the big gossip that went around:. the jock and the brainiac..

265
00:16:55,920 --> 00:17:00,200
From the food trucks,, you could see the cornstalks in back of the movie screen..

266
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:04,040
They covered about a third of the entire field.. The rest of the field was

267
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:08,920
completely surrounded by woods.. As the sun sank lower in the sky,, the tall

268
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:12,720
trees at the entrance to the woods looked dark blue..

269
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:16,319
By the time the other school buses pulled into the parking lots,, we were

270
00:17:16,319 --> 00:17:21,120
back in our spots on the sleeping bags,, right smack in front of the screen:. the

271
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:23,400
best seats in the whole field..

272
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:27,040
Everyone was passing around snacks and having a great time..

273
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:31,240
Me and Jack and Summer and Reed and Maya played Pictionary..

274
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:34,960
We could hear the sound of the other schools arriving,, the loud laughing and

275
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:39,000
talking of kids coming out on the field on both sides of us,, but we couldn’t

276
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,480
really see them..

277
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,960
Though the sky was still light,, the sun had gone down completely, and everything

278
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,280
on the ground had turned deep purple..

279
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:53,000
The clouds were shadows now.. We had trouble even seeing the Pictionary cards in front of us..

280
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:59,440
Just then,, without any announcement,, all the lights at the ends of the field went on at once..

281
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:03,800
They were like big bright stadium lights.. I thought of that scene in Close

282
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:08,600
Encounters when the alien ship lands and they’re playing that music.

283
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,960
Da da doo. Don don.

284
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:18,440
Everyone in the field started applauding and cheering, like something great had just happened.

285
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:22,840
Thanks for watching. please remember to like and subscribe. Become a channel

286
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:27,520
member and we'll see you in The next video.
